3,"Semaq Beri Language (SZC) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/szc/,Semaq Beri is a stable indigenous language of Malaysia. It belongs to the Austro-Asiatic language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Semaq Beri,Austro-Asiatic
4,SEMOQ BERI,https://people-groups.asiaharvest.org/Malaysia/SemoqBeri.pdf,"In the Malaysian Department of Aborigines nomenclature, Semoq Beri refers to a culturally diverse grouping of Orang Asli living in a large area along the eastern and northern tributaries of the Tembeling and Pahang Rivers.",Semaq Beri,Austro-Asiatic
5,Kruspe & Majid: The linguistics of odour in Semaq Beri and ...,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/365832905_The_linguistics_of_odour_in_Semaq_Beri_and_Semelai_two_Austroasiatic_languages_of_the_Malay_Peninsula/fulltext/638609647b0e356feb974510/The-linguistics-of-odour-in-Semaq-Beri-and-Semelai-two-Austroasiatic-languages-of-the-Malay-Peninsula.pdf,"The two focal groups live in far- flung areas of the peninsula: the Semaq Beri in the northeast and the Semelai in the central southwest, and neither group has direct knowledge of the other.",Semaq Beri,Austro-Asiatic
6,Semaq Beri | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/szc/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..RbVxuBe5Jwmv11cBAViO-AsmrbI9jrdz4CyJt1eEt30,Semaq Beri is a stable indigenous language of Malaysia. It belongs to the Austro-Asiatic language family.,Semaq Beri,Austro-Asiatic
7,Semaq Beri - szc (Austro-Asiatic) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/szc/,"Semaq Beri – szc is in the Austro-Asiatic family, included in Austro-Asiatic, Mon-Khmer, Aslian, South Aslian language class.People Groups who primarily speak Semaq Beri. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page.",Semaq Beri,Austro-Asiatic
